y before us!” Joab said, “Let them arise!”","source":"web"},{"ref":"1 Chronicles 13:8","note":"David and all Israel played before God with all their might, even with songs, with harps, with stringed instruments, with tambourines, with cymbals, and with…","source":"web"},{"ref":"2 Chronicles 30:10","note":"So the couriers passed from city to city through the country of Ephraim and Manasseh, even to Zebulun, but people ridiculed them and mocked them.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Job 5:22","note":"You will laugh at destruction and famine, neither will you be afraid of the animals of the earth.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Psalm 2:4","note":"He who sits in the heavens will laugh. The Lord will have them in derision.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Proverbs 1:26","note":"I also will laugh at your disaster. I will mock when calamity overtakes you,","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}